Attribution
-----------

mailboxd is a fork of the Bichon email archiving project, originally
authored by rustmailer.com (https://rustmailer.com,
https://github.com/rustmailer/bichon). The upstream project is
distributed under the same AGPL-3.0-or-later license.

Modifications
-------------

- Renamed the project, binaries, container images, environment
  variables, CLI flags, configuration keys, storage directories and
  HTTP header prefixes from "bichon"/"BICHON_*" to
  "mailboxd"/"MAILBOXD_*".
- Rebranded the web UI, including title, logo references, footer
  and localised strings across all supported languages.
- Removed the upstream release-notification integration against
  github.com/rustmailer/bichon. A replacement pointing at
  git.teccave.de/tecbeat/mailboxd is tracked as a follow-up task.
- Updated deployment artefacts (Dockerfile, systemd unit, example
  environment file, changelog configuration) to reflect the new
  project identity.

The original per-file copyright notices ("Copyright (c) 2025-2026
rustmailer.com") are preserved verbatim in every source file, as
required by AGPL-3.0 § 4 and § 5(b). Every modified file additionally
carries an added "Copyright (c) 2026 tecbeat" line and a modification
notice, as required by AGPL-3.0 § 5(a).

Corresponding source
--------------------

In accordance with AGPL-3.0 § 13, the complete corresponding source
code of this modified version is available at:

    https://git.teccave.de/tecbeat/mailboxd

Users of a running mailboxd instance can find a link to the source
in the web UI footer and on the sign-in screen.

Third-party components
----------------------

mailboxd depends on a number of third-party Rust and JavaScript
libraries. Their respective licenses can be inspected in the
Cargo.lock file, the web/pnpm-lock.yaml file, or generated on demand
with tools such as `cargo about` or `pnpm licenses list`.
